"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[7854],{24181:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"Blur","desc":"Tweens the shared UI background blur. The module returns the tween\\nfunction directly:\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal Blur = require(ReplicatedFirst.Util.Blur)\\n\\nBlur(0, 20)      -- blur in over the default 1s\\nBlur(20, 0, 0.3) -- and back out, faster\\n```\\n\\nOne `BlurEffect` named `UIBlur` is created under Lighting at require time\\nand reused forever \u2014 callers never create their own.\\n\\n### Why the Id child\\n\\nOverlapping calls have to cancel cleanly, and Roblox gives no \\"is this\\ntween still the current one\\" check. So the effect carries a `StringValue`\\nnamed `Id`. Each call writes a fresh random id into it, and a listener on\\nthat value cancels the previous tween whenever the id changes. The call\\nthen yields one `RunService.Stepped` before building its own tween, which\\nis what gives that listener a chance to run.\\n\\n:::caution Yields\\nThat one-frame wait means this function yields. It is brief, but it is\\nreal \u2014 do not call it from a context that must return synchronously.\\n:::\\n\\n`from` is applied to the blur immediately, before the wait, so the tween\\nalways starts from a known size rather than wherever the last cancelled\\ntween happened to stop. Returns the `Tween` (already playing), or nil if\\neither bound was omitted.\\n\\n:::note\\nThis is the low-level tween. `ClientState.activeBlurs` is the higher-level\\nbookkeeping of which UI layers currently want a blur; the two are not\\nwired together here.\\n:::\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/survival-islands - proprietary and confidential.","realm":["Client"],"source":{"line":46,"path":"src/Client/Util/Blur.luau"}}')}}]);